# ConnectIt TODOs

Swept from `// TODO` comments in Source/ConnectIt on 2026-08-14. Each entry
below is the original comment's location plus what investigating it found --
not just a restatement of the one-liner.

## Live pipeline (_ConnectItNetworked)

- [open] AConnectIt_PlayerController.cpp:92 -- ServerRouteBoardChangeRequest_Implementation
  only stamps Request.FactionID from the server-authoritative
  ParticipantComponent->GetActiveParticipantSlotIndex() when the incoming
  value is < 0. Every current action (PlacePiece/Shift/TutorialShiftIntro)
  already sets FactionID >= 0 itself before the RPC ever fires, so this
  "stamp if unset" path is dead in practice -- and more importantly, it
  means the server currently trusts whatever FactionID a client sends as
  long as it's >= 0, only checking that it's *that participant's turn*, not
  that the FactionID actually matches them. A modified client could submit
  a different faction's ID and have it accepted. Fix is likely to stamp
  FactionID from ParticipantComponent unconditionally, not just when unset.

- [open] ConnectIt_TileStateInterpreter.cpp:108 -- FindTileActor unconditionally
  returns nullptr (the TODO explains why: "removed the mapping from
  subsystem and placed on different component", with the old
  GridSub->GetTileAtPosition(Position) call commented out just above).
  This makes SendTagToTile a permanent no-op -- ProcessTileChange still
  correctly detects tile-active/occupation/multiplier changes, but no
  ConnectIt.Tile.* gameplay tag ever actually reaches a tile actor through
  this interpreter, so tiles get no visual feedback from it. The
  replacement mapping already exists:
  UGridTileRegistryComponent::GetTileAtPosition(FGridPosition) (confirmed
  present, Plugins/UnrealGridMechanics/.../Tile/GridTileRegistryComponent.h) --
  same registry AConnectIt_BoardManager::GetTileRegistry() already exposes
  and every other position<->tile lookup in the project now goes through.

- [open] PieceControlInfluenceMap.cpp:26 -- confirmed real bug, not just a
  stale comment. Update() computes Count += TileData->FactionPiece ==
  Snapshot.FactionTurn ? 1 : -1 per neighboring tile. FConnectItBoardState
  ::FactionTurn defaults to -1 (ConnectIt_Structs.h:51) and grepping every
  assignment of FactionTurn project-wide shows it's only ever set inside
  the MinMax/AI tree-search code (simulated hypothetical states, not the
  real board) -- never in ConnectIt_BoardStateComponent/ConnectIt_BoardManager,
  where the live snapshot actually gets built. So on the real board,
  Snapshot.FactionTurn is permanently -1. -1 is also FConnectItTileData's
  "empty" sentinel (FactionPiece == -1), so every empty neighboring tile
  currently scores as if it belonged to the active faction, and every
  occupied tile (any faction, including the active one) scores as
  opposing. The influence map is not measuring what it's meant to. Needs
  Snapshot.FactionTurn actually populated from the real active
  participant/faction before this comparison means anything.

## Legacy / non-networked _ConnectIt (may be moot -- see note below)

- [open] ConnectIt_GameViewModel.h:25 -- PlacePiece "will need to work with
  animations etc." Likely already superseded: the networked pipeline
  solved exactly this ("commit state, then let visuals react") via
  AConnectIt_BoardManager's gated visual sequencing
  (UConnectIt_BoardSequencerComponent + UGameEventTaskSubsystem tag
  sequences) built earlier this session. Worth closing this out once it's
  confirmed nothing still calls this ViewModel path.

- [open] ConnectIt_PlayerData.cpp:10 -- AddToScore has no callback/delegate
  when a player's score changes. Same likely-superseded situation as
  above -- the networked pipeline already broadcasts
  ConnectIt_Event_LineScored with PointsScored on FConnectItBoardChangeEvent.

- [open] ConnectIt_GameFacade.h:39 -- GetGridTiles() returns TArray<AGridTileBase*>
  by value; TODO asks whether it should return a const array instead.
  Minor API-design question, not a functional issue.

- [open] ConnectIt_GameFacade.h:49 -- GetGridTilesWithPlayerPieces(int32 PlayerID)
  "logic messy... should probably also pass in player data not ID". Minor
  API-design question, not a functional issue.

- [open] ConnectIt_GameFacade.h:67 -- GetAllPlayerData() returns raw
  UConnectIt_PlayerData* pointers to live objects, so callers can mutate
  through them even though the class's own doc comment says it exists for
  "access[ing] information about the game without being able to change
  anything" -- the TODO notes the old BP version cloned the data before
  returning it specifically to prevent this. Real gap between documented
  contract and actual behavior, if this facade is still in use.

- [open] ConnectIt_State_Game.cpp:70 -- BroadCastGameState has an
  unresolved debugging question ("why is this not working? Because not Tag
  set?") plus a commented-out `// return;` right below it, suggesting the
  function was fully short-circuited at some point while chasing this and
  only partially reverted. Whether GameState->GetGameStateTag() can return
  an unset tag for some state, and what that does to bound listeners, was
  never confirmed. Needs runtime testing in whatever still exercises this
  legacy state machine.

## Dead / example code (lowest priority)

- [open] ConcreteMinMaxExample.h:159 -- inside TMinMaxManagerBase2::EvaluateTree,
  hardcodes -FLT_MAX/FLT_MAX alpha-beta bounds instead of taking them as
  parameters. The entire file is commented-out reference/example code (not
  compiled, not referenced anywhere) -- only relevant if this example is
  promoted to real code later.

- [open] ConnectIt_MinMaxManager.cpp:180 -- "testing if this works..." left
  on the one delegate assignment (IsGameOverDelegate) made in the
  constructor. Reads like a leftover exploratory note rather than an
  active concern. BuildChildrenDelegate/MoveOrdererDelegate/EvaluatorDelegate
  aren't assigned in this constructor at all -- worth a quick check that
  that's intentional (set elsewhere / not needed here) rather than an
  oversight, then just delete the comment.

- [open] ConnectIt_GridPiece.h:55 -- suggests renaming OnFactionVisualUpdate
  to Initialize_Internal. Confirmed accurate: ConnectIt_GridPiece.cpp calls
  it from both InitialisePiece (server, immediately on pool retrieval) and
  OnRep_FactionID (clients, on replication) -- so the current name implies
  "fires on replication" when it actually means "update visuals for this
  faction," called from two different moments. Pure rename, no behavioral
  change.

- [open] ConnectIt_BoardStateComponent.h:75 -- dead, already-commented-out
  convenience wrappers (IsTileValidForPlacement/GetFactionScore) that just
  duplicate GetCurrentState().IsTileValidForPlacement(...)/.GetScore(...).
  The TODO already states the resolution ("remove"); the code just hasn't
  had the commented block deleted yet. Pure cleanup.

- [open] ConnectIt_BoardStateComponent.cpp:47 -- InitialiseBoardState's
  broadcast-on-init call is already commented out, and the TODO explains
  why (levels should start with tiles/pieces already in place; broadcasting
  a "change" at init time is conceptually wrong). This already reflects the
  intended behavior -- the TODO marker itself could be deleted and the
  explanation kept as a permanent comment instead.
